KG42.register("clusters-5a60f88aff2522cc86eb3fa8",{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v142-d-CL002","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","label":"Local surplus/deficit energy trading and the MCP payment obligation for remaining surplus electricity","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Local surplus/deficit energy trading and the MCP payment obligation for remaining surplus electricity","market_meaning":"When EMS support is available and surplus electricity or an electricity deficit exists, an H-MG may sell surplus electricity or purchase electricity by selecting the lower price. For surplus electricity not sold among H-MGs, the retailer purchases it at the MCP. The product scope, the trading behavior, and the unit-price obligation of this remaining-surplus transaction jointly form a procedural candidate. The MCP is a given interface input.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","pricing","activation","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The energy-product scope in R010 for adjacent H-MGs on the same network is used only for the corresponding exchange among H-MGs. R005 additionally has a retailer-trading branch. The explicit obligation to purchase at the MCP is limited to surplus electricity not sold to other H-MGs and cannot be expanded into a unified payment rule for all deficit purchases or for all transactions. The shared R009 provides only the MCP source interface, and its mathematical gap is not filled here.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is energy trading triggered by surplus or deficit electricity-quantity conditions, together with the obligation to purchase remaining surplus. The product, the execution, and the unit-price obligation are complementary. This cluster is assembled according to procedural meaning and does not claim that per-transaction physical delivery or a complete monetary settlement algorithm has been formed.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Defines the local energy product exchanged between adjacent H-MGs on the same network, and retains its scope, which is narrower than retailer trading."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries sale of surplus electricity, purchase under deficit by selecting the lower price, purchase of remaining surplus by the retailer, and the EMS-support condition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplies the unit-price obligation that the MCP applies when the retailer purchases unsold H-MG surplus, and does not expand that obligation into the full settlement rules."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Cites the pricing source of the MCP. Its primary attribution is CL001. Here it only explains the given price interface and does not again claim complete pricing."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN011","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E11"],"rationale":"The surplus/deficit energy product of adjacent H-MGs on the same network is complementary to their exchange behavior and to the EMS conditions. This product scope does not automatically limit or define the retailer's full trading scope."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN012","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e032","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12"],"rationale":"The local MCP is used in judging surplus sales and is explicitly used as the price at which the retailer purchases remaining surplus. Purchase under deficit by selecting the lower price cannot on this basis be interpreted as necessarily settled at the MCP."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN013","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12"],"rationale":"The purchase behavior and the applicable unit-price obligation of the same remaining-surplus transaction are expressed by two chains respectively. A shared citation does not mean that the execution constraint and the payment constraint are the same object."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM006","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R011::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e032","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12"],"rationale":"These citations all refer to the local MCP of this mechanism, and the pricing-chain node is selected as the display representative. The conditions of each transaction and the scopes of the obligations are kept as they are. Unifying the nodes does not create a new scope of price applicability."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G011","category":"unverified_source","description":"The energy product, the trading, and the unit-price obligation all depend on unaudited B citations. The current assembled state only indicates that the candidate assembly holds within the stated procedural scope. It does not indicate that the source or the scientific conclusion has been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e032"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the original citations and the transaction conditions to which the MCP applies, and retain the unverified status of all entries until a subsequent formal source review."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G012","category":"ontology_extension","description":"R005 retains the necessary EMS condition, but there is no approved independent HEMS node. Proposal v141-b-g01-P2 is still pending review. That condition cannot be rewritten as an identity between HEMS and the MO or as a newly added dependency edge.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P2"],"required_work":"Manually review the HEMS proposal. If its communication, equipment-operation, or dispatch responsibilities are to be expressed, the corresponding representation should first be approved and a source-supported binding should be established by C."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G013","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The existing chains give no explicit mapping from the final dispatch to per-transaction delivery, purchased and sold electricity quantities, and monetary totals, and they give no complete conditions for verifying execution. The completion scope of this cluster is limited to the surplus/deficit trading principles and the unit-price obligation for purchasing remaining surplus.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If extension to computable delivery and settlement rules is required, first check the transaction quantities, the billing basis, and the execution conditions, and then have C provide the objects. Complete payment or performance rules cannot be derived from the unit-price statement alone."}]},"rule_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R010","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R005","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R011","33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-230dbf46f02b4bfe","COMP-52e9b8185e689459","COMP-5f20fde124935957","COMP-6057789601b08e93","COMP-89ca1857e29bb0c7","COMP-db24d9fbcd9569b7","KG40-12aedc3eec573697","KG40-20f45ec4bdcbac06"]});
